    57	### 2a. Runtime-set env vars
    58	
    59	The following vars are set **by the Claude Code runtime** in every Bash subprocess — no hook required. They are available in all shell tool calls regardless of whether the SessionStart hook fired:
    60	
    61	| Env var | Value | Notes |
    62	|---|---|---|
    63	| `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` | session UUID | Auto-set since Claude Code **v2.1.132** (per official changelog); the session UUID. Also exported by the SessionStart hook as a belt-and-suspenders fallback when the runtime has not yet set it. |
    64	| `CLAUDE_EFFORT` | `low` / `medium` / `high` / `xhigh` / `max` | Current effort level for this session. |
    65	| `CLAUDECODE` | `1` | Set to `1` inside Claude Code Bash subprocesses; useful for "am I running inside Claude" detection. |
    66	| `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE` | `"true"` or unset | `"true"` in web/remote deployments; unset locally. |
